workItems.description:
Write the data layer behind its contract: entry/src/main/ets/model/CalculatorStore.ets, entry/src/main/ets/model/HistoryStore.ets, entry/src/main/ets/model/SettingsStore.ets already declare every method the screens call (the app spec's Data layer section), each with a stub body marked TODO(factory). Write every body, and init, which opens what the store keeps (the entry ability awaits it once before the first page; make a second call a no-op). Add private fields, helpers and more files in model/ as you need. Keep every signature exactly as generated: the screens are being written against them at the same time, and the merge is checked for each one. When storage fails, log the error with hilog and rethrow it: a method never resolves as if it had worked (an empty list for a database that did not open, an add that saved nothing), because the screens catch the rejection and show the spec's error states. init may log a failure and return (the entry ability opens the first page either way); a method called on a store whose storage did not open rejects. The entity classes (model/History.ets, model/CalcSettings.ets, model/CalcResult.ets, model/InputEdit.ets) are yours to extend; keep their Data interface, toJSON and fromJSON in step with the fields. A method that returns a ResourceColor gives a colour that belongs to the data (a category's): add each colour to resources/base/element/color.json and resources/dark/element/color.json under a name that starts with the store's, and return $r('app.color.<name>'). A method that returns a Resource gives a text the screens show as it is: add each text to resources/base/element/string.json under a name that starts with the store's, and return $r('app.string.<name>') (a value inside the text is an argument: "Filter: %s" and $r('app.string.<name>', summary)). Write no text a user reads in English in the data layer, not even where the contract returns a string (a formatted date, a label inside a longer value): take it from the resources with the context init received, this.context.resourceManager.getStringByNameSync('<name>', ...args), and a count with getIntPluralStringByNameSync('<name>', n, n) (plurals in resources/base/element/plural.json); by name, not by $r(…).id: the unit tests run the store inside the test HAP, which numbers the same resources differently, so an id fails there ("Invalid resource ID"), and a fallback text in English is the hard-coded string again. Bring unit tests: a hypium suite (a *.test.ets file with a default export, under entry/src/ohosTest/ets/test/model/; expect(x) has assertEqual, assertDeepEquals, assertTrue, assertFalse, assertNull, assertUndefined, assertContain, assertLarger, assertLess, assertClose, assertThrowError and the assertPromise… family; negate one with expect(x).not().assertEqual(y) (there is no assertNotEqual: a test file that does not compile runs no case)) with at least three cases over the operations the screens call (create and read back, update, delete), a case for each rule the spec states (a boundary, an order, a rounding, an unknown id), and persistence: a second store, `const fresh = new <Store>(); await fresh.init(context);`, finds what the first one saved (getInstance() returns the same object, so reading back through it proves nothing about storage). Each case asserts what its name says, and leaves the data as it found it: the suites run against the app's real storage on the device, so delete what a case added in afterEach. The orchestrator runs every suite on the device after the merge, and a failed case comes back to you.

Persistence calls for this app, each compiled with this SDK and run on a device: write from them, they need no lookup.
```ts
import { preferences } from '@kit.ArkData';
import type { common } from '@kit.AbilityKit';
// Preferences (key-value; keep a list as one JSON string). Each entity class in model/ has toJSON (JSON.stringify calls it) and fromJSON
const prefs: preferences.Preferences = preferences.getPreferencesSync(context, { name: 'app_prefs' });   // context: common.Context; open once, share the instance
const raw = prefs.getSync('items', '[]') as string;
const parsed: Object = JSON.parse(raw) as Object;                   // in try/catch: a damaged value is an empty list, not a crash
const items: Item[] = Array.isArray(parsed) ? (parsed as ItemData[]).map((d: ItemData) => Item.fromJSON(d)) : [];
prefs.putSync('items', JSON.stringify(items)); await prefs.flush(); // a value is only on disk after flush()
prefs.deleteSync('items'); await prefs.flush();
// The hypium suite (a store needs a context; take it inside beforeAll, and take the application context: RelationalStore refuses the bare getAppContext() with "Illegal context")
import { beforeAll, describe, expect, it } from '@ohos/hypium';
import { abilityDelegatorRegistry } from '@kit.TestKit';
export default function storeTest() {
  describe('Store', () => {
    let context: common.Context;
    beforeAll(async () => { context = abilityDelegatorRegistry.getAbilityDelegator().getAppContext().getApplicationContext(); /* open the stores here */ });
    it('adds_and_reads_back', 0, async () => { expect(rows.length).assertEqual(1); expect(total).assertLarger(3.9); });
  });
}
```
